3. Training data  --  MIXED, AND PART OF IT IS NON-COMMERCIAL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No dataset is redistributed here; data/raw, data/preprocessed and runs/ are all
gitignored. But **docs/EarLandmarker_web.onnx IS tracked**, and it is a model
trained on all four sources below.

| source      | samples | licence                            | commercial use |
|-------------|---------|------------------------------------|----------------|
| collectionB |   3,153 | iBUG: non-commercial research only | NO             |
| collectionA |     605 | iBUG: non-commercial research only | NO             |
| AudioEar2D  |   2,000 | CC BY 4.0                          | yes, attribute |
| AudioEar3D  |     112 | CC BY 4.0                          | yes, attribute |

AudioEar (Huang et al., AAAI 2023) is CC BY 4.0, confirmed on its Zenodo record
(https://zenodo.org/records/7592895). Permissive; attribution required.

The iBUG ear data (Zhou & Zaferiou, "Deformable Models of Ears in-the-wild",
FG 2017, https://ibug.doc.ic.ac.uk/resources/ibug-ears/) states:

    "The dataset is available for non-commercial research purposes only."

    "You agree not to reproduce, duplicate, copy, sell, trade, resell or
    exploit for any commercial purposes, any portion of the annotations and
    ANY PORTION OF DERIVED DATA."

    "You agree not to further copy, publish or distribute any portion of
    annotations of the dataset."

"Any portion of derived data" reaches trained model weights. **So
docs/EarLandmarker_web.onnx cannot be offered under Apache-2.0's grant of
commercial use.** 64% of the training samples carry that restriction, and it
also requires citing the source databases (VGG Face, LFW, Helen).

Identification basis: these sources use iBUG's exact 55-point scheme, verified
against the iBUG page, and collectionA's 605 samples match its documented
Collection A count. The raw data is not on this machine, so if collectionA/B
turn out to have a different provenance this section should be revisited.

WHAT THIS MEANS IN PRACTICE
  - The SOURCE CODE in this repository is Apache-2.0 and unaffected.
  - The TRAINED WEIGHTS in docs/EarLandmarker_web.onnx are, on this reading,
    non-commercial. Treat them as research-use only until resolved.

Ways to resolve, none of which this file chooses:
  - keep Apache-2.0 for code and mark the weights non-commercial (dual terms);
  - retrain on the CC BY 4.0 sources alone -- 2,112 samples instead of 5,870,
    which would cost accuracy but yield distributable weights;
  - remove the weights from the repository and have users train their own;
  - seek written permission from iBUG.
